WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:01.801
Reason number two

00:00:01.801 --> 00:00:02.135
that I'm

00:00:02.135 --> 00:00:02.502
running is

00:00:02.502 --> 00:00:04.070
because we cannot allow Donald Trump

00:00:04.070 --> 00:00:06.139
to be the Republican nominee again.

00:00:06.139 --> 00:00:07.707
We simply can't.

00:00:07.707 --> 00:00:09.843
And the reason we can't, it's

00:00:09.843 --> 00:00:11.845
not only because he'll lose to Joe Biden,

00:00:12.245 --> 00:00:14.280
although that's the first reason.

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:17.250
But the second reason is he let us down.

00:00:18.451 --> 00:00:21.054
Let's be honest about it.

00:00:21.054 --> 00:00:23.590
I stood on those stages in 2016

00:00:23.590 --> 00:00:25.291
and those debates.

00:00:25.291 --> 00:00:26.493
I participated in them.

00:00:26.493 --> 00:00:28.628
I was up here in New Hampshire

00:00:28.628 --> 00:00:30.230
working hard and campaigning

00:00:30.230 --> 00:00:32.732
And I remember the things he said.

00:00:32.732 --> 00:00:33.299
Let's talk

00:00:33.299 --> 00:00:36.603
about just three of his main promises

00:00:37.137 --> 00:00:39.305
from 2016 promise one

00:00:39.839 --> 00:00:42.542
I will repeal and replace Obamacare

00:00:44.511 --> 00:00:46.079
and we came a Republican Congress

00:00:46.079 --> 00:00:47.013
to do it

00:00:47.247 --> 00:00:47.947
we tell everybody

00:00:47.947 --> 00:00:49.716
I was governor of Jersey for eight years

00:00:49.716 --> 00:00:51.751
I didn't have a Republican legislature

00:00:51.751 --> 00:00:54.120
for 5 minutes of those eight years

00:00:54.354 --> 00:00:56.523
I would have given my right arm

00:00:56.523 --> 00:00:57.357
for one week.

00:00:57.357 --> 00:00:58.425
Tom with you

00:00:58.425 --> 00:01:00.660
as Senate president in New Jersey

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:02.462
you would never see that

00:01:02.462 --> 00:01:05.065
we were working for that whole week.

00:01:05.065 --> 00:01:07.801
He had a Republican Congress

00:01:07.801 --> 00:01:09.903
and he did repeal to replace Obamacare.

00:01:10.470 --> 00:01:12.405
And you want to know why

00:01:12.405 --> 00:01:15.041
in the end we lost by one vote.

00:01:15.875 --> 00:01:17.277
One vote.

00:01:17.343 --> 00:01:18.244
Whose vote was it?

00:01:19.312 --> 00:01:20.914
John McCain's?

00:01:20.914 --> 00:01:23.917
And why didn't John McCain vote that way?

00:01:24.384 --> 00:01:27.487
Because Donald Trump from 2015

00:01:27.487 --> 00:01:31.558
forward insulted John McCain

00:01:31.791 --> 00:01:35.128
every chance he had said he wasn't a war

00:01:35.128 --> 00:01:35.962
hero.

00:01:38.231 --> 00:01:40.200
Insulted his time when he ran

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:41.134
for president,

00:01:41.134 --> 00:01:43.203
insulted his service in the Senate,

00:01:43.203 --> 00:01:45.105
went to Arizona and said

00:01:45.105 --> 00:01:46.773
anybody who's a McCain person

00:01:46.773 --> 00:01:48.775
can't be with me.

00:01:49.809 --> 00:01:52.112
His own selfishness

00:01:52.445 --> 00:01:55.148
and self-centeredness

00:01:55.548 --> 00:01:56.483
cost us repeal

00:01:56.483 --> 00:01:58.551
and replace one of Obamacare.

00:01:58.551 --> 00:02:01.321
So we still have Obamacare today.

00:02:01.321 --> 00:02:02.555
Second,

00:02:03.823 --> 00:02:06.159
This is my favorite one

00:02:06.960 --> 00:02:08.828
he's going to build

00:02:08.828 --> 00:02:11.498
the biggest, most beautiful wall

00:02:11.831 --> 00:02:14.734
you have ever seen from one end

00:02:14.734 --> 00:02:16.970
to the border to the next

00:02:16.970 --> 00:02:19.672
And Mexico's going to pay for it.

00:02:21.374 --> 00:02:24.077
Well, let's review the performance

00:02:25.078 --> 00:02:27.614
he built 52

00:02:28.214 --> 00:02:31.484
new miles of wall in four years.

00:02:32.218 --> 00:02:33.720
52 miles

00:02:35.989 --> 00:02:37.891
he says, Now

00:02:38.224 --> 00:02:40.860
reelect me and I'll get it all done.

00:02:40.927 --> 00:02:44.330
Well, if he goes at the same pace,

00:02:45.598 --> 00:02:47.400
that he went his first four years,

00:02:47.400 --> 00:02:50.703
he only needs 110 more years

00:02:51.271 --> 00:02:53.072
as president of the United States

00:02:53.072 --> 00:02:55.475
to finish the entire wall

00:02:55.475 --> 00:02:58.878
And if you are waiting for the first peso

00:02:59.312 --> 00:03:00.113
to be delivered

00:03:00.113 --> 00:03:03.616
from Mexico to even pay for the 52 miles

00:03:04.217 --> 00:03:06.819
that we got, it hadn't come.

00:03:07.320 --> 00:03:08.154
And I will tell you

00:03:08.154 --> 00:03:09.222
back in 20, 15,

00:03:09.222 --> 00:03:11.758
I met with the president of Mexico

00:03:11.958 --> 00:03:14.661
at that time, President Pena Nieto,

00:03:15.461 --> 00:03:16.262
and I asked him

00:03:16.262 --> 00:03:17.263
what he thought about the wall

00:03:17.263 --> 00:03:19.365
and he said, well, we're not big fans.

00:03:19.365 --> 00:03:20.366
He said, But

00:03:20.366 --> 00:03:22.468
it's your side of the border.

00:03:22.468 --> 00:03:23.736
You can do whatever you want,

00:03:23.736 --> 00:03:24.571
but let me promise

00:03:24.571 --> 00:03:25.905
you one thing, Governor.

00:03:25.905 --> 00:03:28.708
We're never, ever, ever paying for

00:03:28.708 --> 00:03:29.642
it, ever.

00:03:31.211 --> 00:03:31.778
And not only

00:03:31.778 --> 00:03:32.979
has he kept that promise,

00:03:32.979 --> 00:03:35.615
but so is his successor, as well.

00:03:35.615 --> 00:03:37.016
And so

00:03:37.650 --> 00:03:38.551
if he said he's going to fix

00:03:38.551 --> 00:03:40.620
the immigration system,

00:03:40.920 --> 00:03:43.623
how's it look, though, to fix to me.

00:03:43.790 --> 00:03:45.058
But worse than that fact

00:03:45.058 --> 00:03:46.259
that he didn't achieve it,

00:03:46.259 --> 00:03:48.995
he never even proposed

00:03:48.995 --> 00:03:50.630
a piece of legislation

00:03:50.630 --> 00:03:54.133
to fix our broken immigration system.

00:03:54.133 --> 00:03:54.567
Promise.

00:03:54.567 --> 00:03:55.768
Number three,

00:03:56.269 --> 00:03:59.005
I am a businessman

00:03:59.005 --> 00:04:00.873
and I will balance the budget

00:04:00.873 --> 00:04:02.442
in four years

00:04:02.442 --> 00:04:05.545
by cutting wasteful Washington spending

00:04:06.980 --> 00:04:08.881
in four years.

00:04:08.881 --> 00:04:13.253
He added $6 trillion to the national debt

00:04:14.254 --> 00:04:16.956
6 trillion in four years.

00:04:17.390 --> 00:04:19.292
He ran up more debt

00:04:19.292 --> 00:04:20.627
in one term

00:04:20.627 --> 00:04:23.263
than any president in American history.

00:04:23.263 --> 00:04:25.698
And we shouldn't be surprised

00:04:25.698 --> 00:04:26.799
when he runs his business.

00:04:26.799 --> 00:04:28.501
Well, that's right.

00:04:28.501 --> 00:04:30.003
And I was just going to give you

00:04:30.003 --> 00:04:30.637
an example of that.

00:04:30.637 --> 00:04:31.537
I'm going to take you on the road

00:04:31.537 --> 00:04:32.338
with me all the time.

00:04:33.439 --> 00:04:35.074
He's teaming up

00:04:35.074 --> 00:04:36.943
because, you know, he had a business.

00:04:36.943 --> 00:04:39.178
He had businesses in New Jersey

00:04:39.178 --> 00:04:40.980
when I was governor.

00:04:41.581 --> 00:04:44.851
He had casinos in Atlantic City,

00:04:45.551 --> 00:04:48.554
and they went bankrupt three times.

00:04:48.821 --> 00:04:50.890
Now, let me ask you something.

00:04:50.890 --> 00:04:53.559
How stupid do you have to be

00:04:54.027 --> 00:04:56.296
to lose money in a casino?

00:04:57.664 --> 00:04:59.632
The only people who lose money

00:04:59.632 --> 00:05:02.702
in the casino are us.

00:05:02.702 --> 00:05:04.170
I remember when I first time

00:05:04.170 --> 00:05:05.305
ever went to Atlantic City,

00:05:05.305 --> 00:05:06.706
my father took me there

00:05:06.706 --> 00:05:09.042
when that city was the only other place

00:05:09.042 --> 00:05:11.444
other than Nevada that had casinos

00:05:12.078 --> 00:05:15.214
and I went in to the casino

00:05:16.015 --> 00:05:17.917
and I was 18 years old.

00:05:17.917 --> 00:05:21.054
So I was allowed to play and I won

00:05:21.654 --> 00:05:24.324
50 bucks playing blackjack.

00:05:24.791 --> 00:05:26.492
I thought I was the hottest thing

00:05:26.492 --> 00:05:27.493
in the world.

00:05:27.560 --> 00:05:28.328
And my father said, Well,

00:05:28.328 --> 00:05:29.896
let's go for a walk outside

00:05:29.896 --> 00:05:31.798
for a little while. Take a break.

00:05:31.798 --> 00:05:32.932
So he took me outside.

00:05:32.932 --> 00:05:34.033
We were walking on the boardwalk

00:05:34.033 --> 00:05:35.034
in Atlantic City,

00:05:35.034 --> 00:05:35.601
and he said,

00:05:35.601 --> 00:05:37.470
I want you to see all you look at all

00:05:37.470 --> 00:05:39.439
these big, beautiful hotels.

00:05:39.439 --> 00:05:39.806
I said, Yeah,

00:05:39.806 --> 00:05:41.908
because they don't build those because

00:05:41.908 --> 00:05:42.475
you win

00:05:45.078 --> 00:05:47.613
but even with that advantage,

00:05:47.613 --> 00:05:48.548
Donald Trump

00:05:48.548 --> 00:05:50.683
had to go bankrupt three times.

00:05:52.051 --> 00:05:53.086
And then I'll give you one story

00:05:53.086 --> 00:05:54.654
for when I was governor,

00:05:54.654 --> 00:05:57.156
when I became governor

00:05:57.390 --> 00:05:59.025
and holed up eating there.

00:05:59.025 --> 00:06:00.226
Okay, Jim,

00:06:00.226 --> 00:06:02.161
because he's going to fall over on this.

00:06:02.161 --> 00:06:03.830
I had $11 billion

00:06:03.830 --> 00:06:05.331
deficit that I inherited

00:06:05.331 --> 00:06:08.034
on a $29 billion budget night.

00:06:09.035 --> 00:06:11.904
11 billion deficit.

00:06:11.904 --> 00:06:14.407
And when this all came out publicly,

00:06:14.407 --> 00:06:15.475
and we were having to try to deal

00:06:15.475 --> 00:06:17.176
with balancing it,

00:06:17.176 --> 00:06:19.712
my friend Donald Trump called me back.

00:06:20.079 --> 00:06:22.715
This is in 2010 with a suggestion

00:06:23.716 --> 00:06:26.486
he said to me, Chris, go bankrupt.

00:06:28.121 --> 00:06:29.622
I certainly understand Donald's

00:06:29.622 --> 00:06:32.992
states are not allowed to go bankrupt.

00:06:33.326 --> 00:06:35.361
And he goes, No, no, I know.

00:06:35.361 --> 00:06:37.430
Just do it anyway.

00:06:37.430 --> 00:06:39.132
He said, it'll be tied up in the courts

00:06:39.132 --> 00:06:40.166
for years,

00:06:40.166 --> 00:06:40.633
he said,

00:06:40.633 --> 00:06:42.034
and then everyone will just remember

00:06:42.034 --> 00:06:43.269
that you fought

00:06:43.269 --> 00:06:45.004
to not have to pay this money.

00:06:45.004 --> 00:06:46.706
And if whenever the courts figure out,

00:06:46.706 --> 00:06:47.440
then they figure it out.

00:06:47.440 --> 00:06:48.875
But you look like a winner.

00:06:50.743 --> 00:06:52.812
That was his suggestion to me.

00:06:53.012 --> 00:06:55.948
So should we be surprised that he ran up

00:06:55.948 --> 00:06:59.886
$6 trillion in debt in four years?

00:07:00.153 --> 00:07:01.020
And what do you think

00:07:01.020 --> 00:07:01.821
he'll do

00:07:01.821 --> 00:07:05.658
when he never has to answer to you again?

00:07:05.992 --> 00:07:07.460
He's got four years to do

00:07:07.460 --> 00:07:09.529
whatever he wants.

00:07:10.863 --> 00:07:14.100
See, I'm for many of his policies.

00:07:14.400 --> 00:07:15.701
I remember

00:07:15.701 --> 00:07:17.904
I was the first one to endorse him

00:07:17.904 --> 00:07:20.373
after he dropped out of the race.

00:07:20.373 --> 00:07:23.409
I chaired his transition.

00:07:23.709 --> 00:07:25.111
I chaired his opioid and drug

00:07:25.111 --> 00:07:26.712
abuse commission.

00:07:27.213 --> 00:07:28.381
So keep you up at night.

00:07:28.381 --> 00:07:29.148
I played Hillary

00:07:29.148 --> 00:07:32.251
Clinton in debate prep in 2016.

00:07:33.753 --> 00:07:37.023
Was oh yes

00:07:37.490 --> 00:07:37.690
you know

00:07:37.690 --> 00:07:41.294
I'll make your comments later and

00:07:41.294 --> 00:07:43.863
in 2020 I played Joe

00:07:43.863 --> 00:07:45.698
Biden in debate prep

00:07:45.698 --> 00:07:48.000
I took a couple of sedatives before I did

00:07:48.000 --> 00:07:48.734
but I did

00:07:50.903 --> 00:07:51.504
so I'm not

00:07:51.504 --> 00:07:53.539
some never Trumper

00:07:54.807 --> 00:07:56.642
I am against him

00:07:56.642 --> 00:07:59.312
because he let us down on the issues

00:07:59.512 --> 00:08:02.081
that he made us the biggest promises on

00:08:04.550 --> 00:08:06.853
if you like Donald Trump's policies

00:08:07.620 --> 00:08:10.389
why in the hell would you ever hire him

00:08:10.690 --> 00:08:13.059
to make sure they happened.

00:08:13.059 --> 00:08:15.127
He's already proven he can't do it.

00:08:15.862 --> 00:08:16.963
And if you think next

00:08:16.963 --> 00:08:18.297
time is going to be easier than last

00:08:18.297 --> 00:08:18.898
time,

00:08:20.032 --> 00:08:22.568
I will tell you no chance

00:08:22.568 --> 00:08:25.404
because of all of his other conduct.

00:08:25.471 --> 00:08:27.840
So I want to be clear

00:08:27.840 --> 00:08:30.142
that I oppose him

00:08:30.743 --> 00:08:33.212
for his incompetence.

00:08:33.312 --> 00:08:35.615
I oppose him for his broken promises

00:08:36.482 --> 00:08:38.551
before we ever get

00:08:38.551 --> 00:08:40.052
any of the criminal indictments.

